---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { products, site } from '../data/site';

const description =
  'Beastry 的共建前门：从 GitHub 读取想法、兴趣和已合并的贡献。提交、表态和留言都在 GitHub 上完成。';
const descriptionEn =
  'Beastry’s front door for making things together. Ideas, interest, and merged contributions are read from GitHub. Submitting, reacting, and commenting happen on GitHub.';

const storyIssue = 'https://github.com/Beastry/ideas/issues/new?title=%5BStory%5D%20';
const beasts = 'https://github.com/Beastry/brand/blob/main/guidelines/04-fable-beasts.md';
---

<Base title="共建" titleEn="Make together" description={description} descriptionEn={descriptionEn}>
  <article class="page">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker"><span lang="zh-Hans">社区</span><span lang="en">Community</span></p>
      <h1><span lang="zh-Hans">一起做成 Beastry</span><span lang="en">Make Beastry together</span></h1>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        Beastry 的品牌来自一起做出来的软件、角色和故事。这一页是前门：打开时向 GitHub 读取公开记录，再把提交、表态和留言交回 GitHub。本站没有账号，没有论坛，也不把投票存在这里。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        The Beastry brand comes from software, characters, and stories made together. This page is the front door. It reads the public GitHub record when you open it, then sends submitting, reacting, and commenting back to GitHub. There is no account, no forum, and no vote stored here.
      </p>

      <h2><span lang="zh-Hans">社区提案和正式资产</span><span lang="en">Community proposals and official assets</span></h2>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        GitHub Issue 是社区提案。正式产品在
        <a href="/projects">项目</a>。母品牌的粉兔、蓝猫、黄熊写在
        <a href={beasts} rel="noreferrer">Beastry/brand 的寓言三兽</a>，各产品的标志在各自仓库。提案在维护者另行决定之前，不是正式资产。本站没有权利转让表单。提交一条 Issue 不表示把权利转给 Beastry。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        A GitHub issue is a community proposal. Official products are on
        <a href="/projects">Projects</a>. The mother brand’s pink rabbit, blue cat, and yellow bear are in
        <a href={beasts} rel="noreferrer">Beastry/brand’s fable beasts</a>. Each product’s mark stays in its own repository. A proposal is not an official asset unless a maintainer decides that later. This site has no assignment form. Opening an issue does not transfer rights to Beastry.
      </p>

      <h2><span lang="zh-Hans">三条路</span><span lang="en">Three paths</span></h2>
      <div class="path-grid">
        <section class="path-card">
          <h3><span lang="zh-Hans">软件</span><span lang="en">Software</span></h3>
          <p lang="zh-Hans">Beastry/ideas 有 Idea 模板。点开会到 GitHub，用你自己的 GitHub 账号提交。</p>
          <p lang="en">Beastry/ideas has an Idea template. The button opens GitHub, and you submit with your own GitHub account.</p>
          <p><a class="button primary" href={site.ideaIssue} rel="noreferrer"><span lang="zh-Hans">在 GitHub 上打开 Idea 模板</span><span lang="en">Open the Idea template on GitHub</span></a></p>
        </section>
        <section class="path-card">
          <h3><span lang="zh-Hans">角色、故事、社区创作</span><span lang="en">Character, story, community work</span></h3>
          <p lang="zh-Hans">没有单独的模板，也没有已启用的品牌资产通道。这个链接只在 GitHub 的空白 Issue 里预填标题 <code>[Story]</code>。它仍是一条讨论，不是正式标志。</p>
          <p lang="en">There is no separate template and no open channel for official brand assets. This link only prefills the title <code>[Story]</code> on GitHub’s blank issue form. It remains a discussion, not an official mark.</p>
          <p><a class="button ghost" href={storyIssue} rel="noreferrer"><span lang="zh-Hans">在 GitHub 上写一条故事 Issue</span><span lang="en">Open a story issue on GitHub</span></a></p>
        </section>
        <section class="path-card">
          <h3><span lang="zh-Hans">已有产品</span><span lang="en">An existing product</span></h3>
          <p lang="zh-Hans">任务在该产品自己的 Issues。认领就是在那条 Issue 下留言。代码用 Pull Request 交回同一个仓库。</p>
          <p lang="en">Tasks are that product’s own issues. A claim is a comment on the issue. Code comes back as a pull request to the same repository.</p>
          <p><a class="button ghost" href="#tasks"><span lang="zh-Hans">看下面的任务入口</span><span lang="en">See the task links below</span></a></p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <h2 id="ideas"><span lang="zh-Hans">正在收集的想法</span><span lang="en">Ideas being collected</span></h2>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        列表在页面打开时从 <a href={`${site.ideas}/issues`} rel="noreferrer">Beastry/ideas</a> 读取。+1 是 GitHub 反应，只表示兴趣，不自动提高优先级。维护者决定做什么。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        The list is read from <a href={`${site.ideas}/issues`} rel="noreferrer">Beastry/ideas</a> when the page opens. A +1 is a GitHub reaction. It signals interest and does not raise priority by itself. A maintainer decides what happens next.
      </p>
      <div id="idea-board">
        <p lang="zh-Hans">实时列表由页面打开后向 GitHub 读取。读不到时，记录仍在上面的 Issues 链接里。</p>
        <p lang="en">The live list is requested from GitHub after the page opens. If that read fails, the record is still at the issues link above.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="tasks"><span lang="zh-Hans">可以接手的任务</span><span lang="en">Tasks you can take</span></h2>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        本站不维护任务副本。下面先列出各仓库的 Issues 和已有文档。再向 GitHub 查询当前带有 <code>help wanted</code> 或 <code>good first issue</code> 的打开 Issue。没有结果就显示没有。要表示你在做，请在该 Issue 下留言，写明范围和你会怎样验证。留言留在 GitHub。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        This site does not keep a copy of the tasks. The repository links come first. The page then asks GitHub for open issues that currently carry <code>help wanted</code> or <code>good first issue</code>. No result means none. To say you are doing the work, comment on that issue with the scope and how you will verify it. The comment stays on GitHub.
      </p>
      <ul class="help-list">
        {
          products.map((product) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{product.name}</h3>
              <p class="project-links">
                <a href={`${product.github}/issues`} rel="noreferrer">Issues</a>
                {' · '}
                <a href={`${product.github}/pulls`} rel="noreferrer">Pull requests</a>
                {product.extraLinks?.map((link) => (
                  <>
                    {' · '}
                    <a href={link.href} rel={link.href.startsWith('http') ? 'noreferrer' : undefined}>
                      <span lang="zh-Hans">{link.zh}</span>
                      <span lang="en">{link.en}</span>
                    </a>
                  </>
                ))}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <div id="task-board">
        <p lang="zh-Hans">带标签的任务在页面打开后向 GitHub 查询。</p>
        <p lang="en">Labeled tasks are requested from GitHub after the page opens.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="delivered"><span lang="zh-Hans">已经交回的贡献</span><span lang="en">Contributions already handed back</span></h2>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        这里读取 GitHub 上已合并的 Pull Request。它证明有人把改动交回了仓库，不证明该作品已被收成正式品牌资产，也不转移权利。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        This reads merged pull requests from GitHub. A merged change shows that work was handed back to a repository. It does not show that the work was adopted as an official brand asset, and it does not transfer rights.
      </p>
      <div id="pull-board">
        <p lang="zh-Hans">已合并的记录在页面打开后向 GitHub 查询。</p>
        <p lang="en">Merged records are requested from GitHub after the page opens.</p>
      </div>

      <h2><span lang="zh-Hans">谁可以做这些操作</span><span lang="en">Who can take these actions</span></h2>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        提交、+1 和留言都要用一个对这次工作负责的人的 GitHub 账号。代理可以准备文字，由这个人在 GitHub 上发出。合并、发布和权限仍由仓库维护者决定。说明在
        <a href="/agents">给代理的说明</a>。公开索引在 <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        Submitting, adding +1, and commenting use the GitHub account of a person who is responsible for that work. An agent can draft the words. That person sends them on GitHub. Merges, releases, and permissions stay with the repository maintainer. The notes are in
        <a href="/agents">For agents</a>. The public index is <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>.
      </p>
      <p lang="zh-Hans">
        未登录的读取大约每小时 60 次，搜索大约每分钟 10 次，按来访者的网络计算。到上限时，列表会说明读不到，GitHub 链接仍可用。写信：
        <a href="mailto:community@beastry.app">community@beastry.app</a>。
      </p>
      <p lang="en">
        Unsigned reads are about 60 an hour, and searches about 10 a minute, counted for the visitor’s network. At the limit, the list says it could not be read, and the GitHub links still work. Write to
        <a href="mailto:community@beastry.app">community@beastry.app</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  import { loadCommunity, renderIdeas, renderPulls, renderTasks, type BoardState, type Lang } from '../lib/cocreate';

  const ideaBoard = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#idea-board');
  const taskBoard = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#task-board');
  const pullBoard = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#pull-board');
  let state: BoardState | null = null;

  function language(): Lang {
    return document.documentElement.dataset.lang === 'en' ? 'en' : 'zh';
  }

  function paint() {
    const lang = language();
    if (!state || !ideaBoard || !taskBoard || !pullBoard) return;
    ideaBoard.innerHTML = renderIdeas(state.ideas, lang);
    taskBoard.innerHTML = renderTasks(state.tasks, lang);
    pullBoard.innerHTML = renderPulls(state.pulls, lang);
  }

  loadCommunity(fetch)
    .then((next) => {
      state = next;
      paint();
    })
    .catch(() => {
      state = { ideas: { status: 'unavailable' }, tasks: { status: 'unavailable' }, pulls: { status: 'unavailable' } };
      paint();
    });

  new MutationObserver(paint).observe(document.documentElement, {
    attributes: true,
    attributeFilter: ['data-lang'],
  });
</script>
